# Miqra App — Project Context (Lean v2.2)
> Minimal context so Cursor always generates Flutter + Riverpod + Supabase code in Rahmah UX style.

## Stack
- Flutter 3.x (Material/Cupertino), Dart null-safety
- State: Riverpod (+ hooks)
- Backend: Supabase (Postgres, Auth, Storage, Realtime) + RLS
- Local cache: Isar/SQLite
- Monitoring: Sentry, Analytics: PostHog
- Design: Rahmah UX (calm, minimal, ethical)

## Architecture
- Feature-first folders; keep modules independent
- Local-first → sync later (no hard fails offline)
- One primary action per screen; reduce UI noise
- Avoid over-abstraction; prefer composition

## Security & Privacy
- Enforce RLS: `auth.uid()` on all user tables
- Reflections/dua private by default; encrypt locally
- No secrets in code; signed URLs with short expiry
- No random rewards / gambling-like mechanics

## Rahmah UX (only what impacts code)
- Calmer feedback (no guilt): use soft states, timeouts ≤ 250ms
- Typography: Amiri (Arabic), Inter (Latin) if applicable
- Colors (tokens only): turquoise, coral, gold, sand
- Large tap targets; accessible contrast; support RTL

## Performance
- Minimize rebuilds (HookConsumerWidget, const where possible)
- Lazy-load Qur’an data; paginate streams
- Profile with `--profile`; avoid heavy animations

## Output expectations
- Riverpod providers for state
- Repositories/services for IO
- Small, focused widgets; early returns over deep nesting
- Meaningful names; no magic numbers (use constants)

# End
